  "paraphrase": "Princess Märtha Louise of Norway, who claims to have psychic abilities and is the daughter of one of Europe's most enduring monarchs, wed Durek Verrett, a California-based man who identifies as a sixth-generation spiritual healer, on Saturday afternoon. Despite the unconventional nature of this royal wedding, onlookers gathered along the cloudy streets of Geiranger hoping to see the bride. The 52-year-old princess, who holds fourth position in Norway's line of succession as the sole daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, exchanged vows with the 49-year-old Verrett in a traditional Norwegian church service. The ceremony took place at the four-star Hotel Union, located in a small community below the Geiranger fjord, with royal family members and famous personalities in attendance. Seven bridesmaids accompanied the princess, including her teenage daughters Leah and Emma Behn from her previous marriage to late Norwegian writer Ari Behn, from whom she divorced in 2017. The wedding guests, numbering 350, included her brother Crown Prince Haakon with Crown Princess Mette-Marit, Sweden's Crown Princess Victoria and Prince Daniel, plus Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien from the Netherlands. The princess has led an unconventional royal existence, having previously proclaimed her clairvoyant abilities and operating a healing academy for a decade where she instructed others in angelic communication. In 2022, she declared her intention to resign from formal royal responsibilities to concentrate on her and Verrett's commercial ventures and create clearer separation between their activities and Norway's royal family. Verrett presents himself on social media as a 'divine servant' and 'energy practitioner,' counting Goop's founder Gwyneth Paltrow among his prominent clients, whom he refers to as a 'spiritual sister.'"
